From 61cc8cd544455fc4483f3ae08fe75dc58b2fcd38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 05:24:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] robo(downloads): Reference Sheet shows Reports' own
 figures for the latest batch; robot delays longest-first with a top-3 pie
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Reference Sheet computed Total Slabs Produced, Total Production Time, Total
Delays and Avg Slabs/hour itself, over only the setup rows whose design name
matched the search, and with its own Avg formula (delays subtracted). One batch
is often several setup rows, each with the design typed afresh — D-1445 has
rows typed "calcatta gold" and "CALCATTA GOLD" — so the sheet read 322 (or 37)
slabs where Reports reads 359 for the same batch.

- reportSummary (new): the Reports summary calculation, moved verbatim out of
  the Reports route into one shared function. The Reports route now calls it
  (same queries, same output, same JSON), and so does the Reference Sheet —
  one implementation, so the two screens cannot disagree for a batch.
- referenceData: the design name (case-insensitive, thickness ignored) is used
  only to find the design's latest production batch — the batch of its most
  recently produced slab. The batch is then taken whole through Reports' own
  batch filter (resolveBatchRecipeIds), and the four figures are
  computeReportSummary() for it: exactly what Reports shows for that batch in
  its default "All" mode. Production date is the batch's first slab; robot
  delays cover every delay of the batch (the same rows Total Delays sums);
  programs stay bounded to this design's setups so a mixed batch never lends
  another design's programs.
- referenceSheet: removed the Reference-only Avg formula (avgSlabsPerHourNet)
  and its interval union (mergedDelayMinutes) rather than leave a second
  calculation around; added latestProduced(), robotDelaysByDuration() (one row
  per code, sorted by total duration, longest first; ties in code order) and
  robotDelayPie() (1-3 slices, or the top 3 by duration when there are more,
  with the share of all robot delay time those three cover).
- RobotDelayPie (new): the pie under the Robot Delays table — Recharts loaded
  via next/dynamic like the Reports charts, the Reports' categorical colours
  (checked for colour-blind separation), a 2px gap between slices, the share on
  each slice and a legend naming code, description, duration and share.
- DownloadsClient: the four figures use Reports' labels and format ("Total
  Production Time", "—" for none); the Robot Delays heading says longest first;
  the pie sits below the table.
- tests: design matching for every capitalisation, latest-batch selection,
  duration ordering (the owner's C1/C5/C8 example), pie slicing for 1, 2, 3
  and more types, and a source-level guard that the four figures come from
  Reports' function — mutation-checked to fail if a separate calculation is
  added back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SPqDFZ7o6eq1utS7hzoQsF
