From c84ed1a85b1278da8af4b512569c0315597c7ec4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:32:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] robo(entry): next S.No. and slab number always follow the
 last slab entered, across refresh, navigation and edits

Last slab entered S.No. 13 / slab 161223: the form rightly offered 14 /
161224 while entering, but after a page refresh, a trip to another page and
back, or an edit to an older slab (e.g. 161206) it sometimes offered a wrong
S.No. or slab number.

Root cause: those are exactly the moments the form asks the server for the
next pair (after an ordinary save it counts on from the slab it just wrote,
which is why normal entry was right). The server took "the last row" to be
the newest shift date's HIGHEST S.No. But one shift row carries every batch
set up that day, a long batch keeps running on its shift for days, and a new
batch's S.No. starts again from 1 - so an earlier, longer batch on the same
shift won: 61 offered after 13, and the slab number counted on from that old
row into numbers already used, landing on the first gap.

- registerOrderDb: lastEnteredRows - the newest slabs SAVED on the running
  (ACTIVE) shift, newest first; only if those carry no S.No. or countable
  slab number, the latest shift date's by save time. An edit never changes
  when a slab was saved and nothing in the page's memory takes part, so a
  refresh, navigation or an edit reads the same pair. Imports cannot move it:
  they write onto CLOSED shifts of the register's own dates.
- next-number route and the POST's own S.No. (form sent none) both use it,
  so they cannot disagree; the response is marked no-store.
- RoboEntryForm: its reads are fetched no-store, so a refresh never shows a
  cached pair. The count-on after each save is unchanged.
- tests: the owner's case against an in-memory table honouring the real
  query (13 / 161223 -> 14 / 161224, stable on re-ask), the old reading's
  61 and gap-number shown, an edit to 161206 (even of its S.No.) moving
  nothing, imports before and after the running shift ignored, a new day's
  setup with no slab yet, a row saved without an S.No.; source guards that
  both callers share it. Mutation-checked.

