Remove, so the chosen code showed as "C10 ROBOT" with its description cut
off (or "C10 B... ROBOT"), and the time boxes were too narrow for "10:15".

Layout only - the same fields, values, validation, duration and saving:
- Each delay is three rows at every screen size: 1. Delay code alone,
  full width; 2. Start, End, Duration in three equal columns; 3. Remarks,
  full width. A robot-specific code's Machine(s) picker sits between 2 and
  3; Remove moves to the delay code's label line.
- The chosen code reads in the list's order - code, full description,
  category ("C10 Bowl Dry Cleaning ROBOT") - and a long description wraps
  instead of being truncated; on a phone the category drops beneath it.
- The code list shows every description in full (wrapping), a little taller.
- Touch screens: the Duration box and the chosen-code box match the 44px
  the time inputs already have there; the time boxes get slightly narrower
  side padding so "HH:MM" fits a phone's third of a row.
- Checked rendered at 390, 810, 1180 and 1440 px (touch and mouse): no
  truncated description, no sideways scroll, every control 44px on touch.

